From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanshen Cao <1677399301gg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Feb 2026 09:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: richtek,rt1711h: document Etek ET7304 TCPC

Add the Etek ET7304 as a compatible device in the RT1711H TCPC
binding documentation. The ET7304 is register-compatible with the
Richtek RT1715 and uses a fallback compatible string:

  compatible = "etekmicro,et7304", "richtek,rt1715";

This follows the approach proposed by Alexey Charkov to use
fallback compatibles for TCPCI chips that reimplement RT1711H/RT1715
registers.

Upstream references:
  https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260220-et7304-v3-1-ede2d9634957@gmail.com/
  https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2603.2/05539.html

Signed-off-by: Yuanshen Cao <1677399301gg@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexey Charkov <alchark@gmail.com>
[backport-6.6: adapted for orangepi BSP kernel 6.6.98]
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/richtek,rt1711h.yaml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/richtek,rt1711h.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/richtek,rt1711h.yaml
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/richtek,rt1711h.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/richtek,rt1711h.yaml
@@ -17,9 +17,15 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
       - enum:
           - richtek,rt1711h
           - richtek,rt1715
+      - items:
+          - const: etekmicro,et7304
+          - const: richtek,rt1715
+    description:
+      The Etek ET7304 is register-compatible with Richtek RT1715 and
+      should use "richtek,rt1715" as a fallback compatible.

   reg:
     maxItems: 1
--
2.39.2

